orrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 1}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0", "image": "engenn7le17ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Next year, the city of Cambridge is planning to build a new highway that will run from the east part of the city to the west. The highway should relieve some of the traffic coming downtown from the suburbs. If things go as planned, construction will begin next summer.<br/>\nEnvironmentalists' groups are protesting the construction of this new highway. They say that if the city decided to build it, the pollution level would increase exponentially. John Smits, you are the head of \"Citizens for Green\", a climate change activist group. How do you think we can avoid this environmental issue?", "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le17ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: The city could work on a better public transit system instead of planning more roads. If more people used buses, there would be less traffic and better air for us to breathe. The smog here will be as bad as in Boston if we go ahead with the proposed plan.", "time": "35000", "image": "engenn7le17ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Can you tell us how you are going to put pressure on the city officials?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: We are organizing a protest in front of the city hall on Sunday. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What would you suggest to our listeners if they wanted to get more involved?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John Smits</span>: If we want a better future for our children, we will need to make sure our air stays clean. I wouldn't choose parking lots over green spaces.", "time": "50000", "image": "engenn7le17ob01re2img05.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le17ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le17ob01re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Environmental News", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Issues in the Community", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the first conditional with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> clauses to talk about real possibilities in the future.</p><p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do or not do something. In that condition, something else may, will or will not happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\">If</span> clause and the <span class=\"italic\">Condition</span> clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Second Conditional to talk about hypothetical situations. It's not certain that it's possible to fulfill the condition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No. <br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional:<br/>1st Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional:<br/>2nd Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If things go as planned,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">construction will begin next year.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible that things will  go as planned. In this condition, construction will begin. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we want a better future,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we will need to make sure our air stays clean.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible we will want a better future. In this condition, we will need to make sure our air is clean.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional:<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> ... + Simple Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional:<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span> + base verb</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If the city decided to build the highway, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the pollution level would increase.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is not certain that the city will build the highway. What would happen if it did? The pollution level would increase.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If more people used buses,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">there would be less traffic.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is not certain that more people will use buses. What would happen if they did? There would be less traffic.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Modals for Suggestions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to offer advice or give solutions to a problem, you use modals like <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These modals can go at the beginning of the sentence, or after a clause starting with \u201c<span class=\"italic\">If</span> ...\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modal is followed by a verb in the base form. You do not use \u201c<span class=\"italic\">to</span>\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would / I'd ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I wouldn't ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You could ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You should ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The highway should relieve some of the traffic coming downtown from the suburbs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The city  could  work on a better public transit system instead of planning more roads. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wouldn't choose parking lots over green spaces.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "environmental", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to the impact of human activity on the environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How do you think we can avoid this environmental issue?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about the environment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "suburbs", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the urban area surrounding the downtown core", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The highway should relieve some of the traffic coming downtown from the suburbs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "environmentalist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who advocates the protection of the environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Environmentalists are protesting the construction of this new highway.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "climate change", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a change in global weather patterns largely caused by pollution", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: John Smits is the head of a climate change activist group.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to put pressure on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make demands on someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can you tell us how you are going to put pressure on the city officials?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "smog", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fog or haze combined with smoke and pollution", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The smog here will be as bad as in Boston if we go ahead with the proposed plan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le17ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Make a list of five of the biggest problems facing our environment. Make a short presentation 3 to 5 minutes long discussing these problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make suggestions about some of the things we can do to help the environment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the suggestions with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask for clarification about your partner's suggestions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I  discuss how to deal with problems. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I  talk about cause and effects and hypothetical situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I  ask for clarification.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena"}